Final real-backend run: all three tests, -test.count=3, all PASS.
  TestManualResidencyServiceKvrocks: 3.47s / 3.30s / 3.29s.
    Real hot UNLINK retains cold data; Gateway Service restart while cold;
    syncer process restart with eviction in stream; cold GET and cold INCR;
    GET/INCR/GET pipeline order; eight concurrent INCRs return 47..54 once each;
    stale eviction/rewarming scripts cannot replace newer hot value;
    new-ID one-endpoint preparation/confirmation/eviction; business DEL removes
    cold value too, and subsequent GET does not resurrect it.
    Injected cold connection failure produces TRYAGAIN for a cold INCR while
    a different hot key stays readable; restoring the connection needs no repair.
    Cold outage is a transport fault injection, not a killed Kvrocks process.
    32 KiB String: MEMORY USAGE before=41024 bytes; residency + shared prepare
    marker allocations=1056 bytes. This is per-key allocation, NOT process RSS,
    total system cost, or a guarantee that small values save memory.
  TestBoundedPreparationServiceKvrocks: 1.78s / 1.86s / 1.85s.
    Prior bounded preparation/retained-hot completion regression.
  TestFinishColdCommittedLocalMissingKvrocks: 0.20s / 0.16s / 0.19s.
    Prior exact cold completion/local terminal recovery regression.

Issue found in integration and corrected:
  Segment GC originally assumed one pending item equals one source frame.
  Residency groups can cross segments: retain/prove the first frame through EXEC.

Limitations:
  Internal opt-in only, no public YAML/Proxy cutover or automatic LRU.
  Single-key String subset, no TTL/Cluster/HA/full-resync replacement certification.
  Pipeline is executed one command at a time in this mode for correct miss order.
  Hot writes do not wait for Kvrocks, but use an internal Redis script; latency
  and throughput have NOT been benchmarked. Per-key residency metadata remains.
  Gateway restart is Service teardown/reconstruction, not OS process kill timing.
  No randomized source-reply loss or source-failover certification in this run.

Cleanup: dedicated test containers stopped after the final run; retained for
inspection. No deploy, push, or new implementation commit performed.
